INT. COFFEE SHOP - DAY

A cozy coffee shop with warm lighting. SARAH, 28, sits at a corner table with her laptop. MIKE, 30, enters carrying a briefcase.

MIKE
Sarah! I didn't expect to see you here.

SARAH
(looking up)
Mike? What a surprise!

Mike pulls out a chair and sits down.

MIKE
How have you been? It's been ages.

SARAH
Good, good. Just working on the new project. You know how it is.

MIKE
Tell me about it. The deadline is killing me.

Sarah closes her laptop and leans forward.

SARAH
Maybe we can help each other out. Two heads are better than one.

MIKE
(smiling)
I like the way you think.

EXT. COFFEE SHOP - EVENING

The sun is setting. Sarah and Mike exit the coffee shop together, laughing.

SARAH
Same time tomorrow?

MIKE
You bet. I'll bring the good coffee.

They walk in opposite directions down the street.

INT. SARAH'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

Sarah enters her small but tidy apartment. She tosses her bag on the couch and pulls out her phone.

SARAH
(to herself)
This might actually work.

She dials a number and waits.

VOICE (V.O.)
Hello?

SARAH
Hey, it's me. I think I found a way to solve our problem.

INT. MIKE'S OFFICE - NIGHT

Mike is at his desk, surrounded by papers and coffee cups. His phone rings.

MIKE
(answering)
Mike here.

SARAH (V.O.)
I've been thinking about what we discussed.

MIKE
(interested)
And?

SARAH (V.O.)
Meet me tomorrow. I have a plan.

MIKE
I'll be there.

He hangs up and looks at the papers on his desk with renewed determination.

FADE OUT.
